# Glossary Rules

## File: `web/data/glossary/terms.yaml`

Each entry maps Chinese (`zh`) to **two renderings**:

```yaml
series: default  # or series name
terms:
  - zh: "般若"
    hv: "Bát Nhã"       # Hán-Việt — mandatory for .hv.md (âm dịch)
    vi: "Bát Nhã"       # Thuần Việt — mandatory for .vi.md (readable Vietnamese)
    notes: "Prajna; not 'trí tuệ' alone when technical"
    sanskrit: "prajñā"
```

## Fields

| Field | Layer | Use |
|-------|-------|-----|
| `zh` | lookup | Primary key; use full compound when fixed |
| `hv` | `.hv.md` | Hán-Việt âm dịch — word-by-word reading |
| `vi` | `.vi.md` | Thuần Việt — readable Buddhist register |
| `sanskrit` / `pali` | notes | Optional doctrinal reference |
| `doctrine: true` | both | Requires reviewer sign-off |
| `alt_vi` | vi | Deprecated thuần Việt forms to avoid |
| `status: pending` | — | Block translation until resolved |

## Principles

- **One `zh` → one `hv` and one `vi`** per series scope
- When `hv` and `vi` are the same (proper names, established compounds), set both explicitly
- When layers differ: `hv` stays âm dịch; `vi` uses natural thuần Việt (e.g. 修多羅 hv `Tu Đa La`, vi `kinh`)
- No hyphens in `hv` or `vi`: Title Case syllables (`Bát Nhã Ba La Mật`, `A Nan`); hyphens only in `sanskrit` / `notes`
- Legacy entries with only `vi` are treated as `hv` until curated

## Translation usage

| Output | Use field | Agent / skill |
|--------|-----------|---------------|
| `.hv.md` | `hv` | `/sino-vietnamese-translator`, translate-sino-vietnamese |
| `.vi.md` | `vi` | `/translator`, translate-buddhist-text |

Never substitute `hv` readings in `.vi.md` or `vi` readings in `.hv.md` unless the two fields are identical in the glossary.

## Updates

- New term: add `hv` + `vi` before first use in translation
- Conflict between series: use `series:` scoped files (`web/data/glossary/{series}.yaml`)
- Auto-extract from HV drafts populates `hv`; curator must set `vi` when it differs
